stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (good board of the previous job has left the AOI, so time spent in preparation does not count) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (against the target, but poor preparation is the most common reason for missing the target.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 693 Td (6.1 Timing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 671 Td (The material handler starts preparation when the Atlas shop-floor module shows that the running) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 658 Td (job has 60 minutes or less of remaining build time. The line lead confirms the next job on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 645 Td (Atlas schedule at the same time. If the schedule has been changed by planning in the last 60) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 632 Td (minutes, the line lead must confirm with the shift lead that the new job is correct before any) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 619 Td (material is kitted.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 596 Td (6.2 Kitting) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 574 Td (The material handler kits all component reels, trays and tubes for the next job against the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 561 Td (Atlas pick list. Each reel is scanned out of stores so that the Atlas inventory reflects the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 548 Td (move. Partial reels are preferred over new reels where the partial reel quantity covers the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 535 Td (job, to reduce the number of open reels on the floor.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 512 Td (6.3 Moisture sensitive components) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 490 Td (Moisture sensitive devices \(MSDs\) must be handled according to mfg-msl-handling-procedure. For) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 477 Td (the Penang lines the most common level is MSL 3, which has a floor life of 168 hours once the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 464 Td (dry pack is opened. Before an MSL 3 reel is kitted, the material handler checks the floor life) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 451 Td (label. If the accumulated exposure exceeds 168 hours, the reel must be baked according to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 438 Td (mfg-msl-handling-procedure before it can be used. Do not kit an expired reel "to be baked) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 425 Td (later"; baked reels are kitted as a separate delivery.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 402 Td (6.4 Solder paste) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 380 Td (Solder paste is SAC305 Type 4. Unopened jars are stored in the paste refrigerator at 2\22610 \260C.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 367 Td (The material handler removes the paste required for the next job from the refrigerator and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 354 Td (allows it to thaw for at least 4 hours at room temperature before opening. Opening a jar before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 341 Td (it has thawed causes condensation in the paste and leads to solder balling.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 319 Td (Once a jar is opened on the line it may stay open for a maximum of 24 hours. The time the jar) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 306 Td (was opened is written on the jar label. Paste that has been open for more than 24 hours must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 293 Td (scrapped, not returned to the refrigerator. Paste left on the stencil at the end of a job may) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 280 Td (be reused on the next job only if the next job is on the same line, the paste is within its) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 267 Td (24-hour open time, and it has not been contaminated.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 244 Td (6.5 Pre-staging feeders offline) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 222 Td (Feeders for the next job are loaded offline on the feeder cart at the pre-staging bench. Each) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 209 Td (reel is loaded into a feeder, the feeder barcode and the reel barcode are scanned together at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 196 Td (the pre-staging bench, and the pairing is recorded in the Atlas shop-floor module. Pre-staged) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 183 Td (carts are labelled with the line, the job number and the placement machine they are intended) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 170 Td (for.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 147 Td (6.6 Stencil and program readiness) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 125 Td (The line lead retrieves the stencil for the next job from the stencil store and checks:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 103 Td (- The stencil ID matches the traveller \(format STN-<board>-<rev>\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 90 Td (- The stencil tension is at least 35 N/cm at all five measurement points. A stencil below 35) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 77 Td (   N/cm at any point is quarantined and reported to the process engineer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 64 Td (- The apertures are clean and undamaged when viewed on the light table.) Tj ET
endstream
