BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (The line lead also confirms that the placement programs for both placement machines, the SPI) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (program, the AOI program and the reflow profile named on the traveller are available on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (line PC. The profile is not loaded yet.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 680 Td (6.7 ESD readiness) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 658 Td (All personnel involved in the changeover must pass the wrist strap check at the station tester) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 645 Td (before touching boards, feeders or stencils, per mfg-esd-control-standard. A failed wrist strap) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 632 Td (check must be resolved before the person takes part in the changeover.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 607 Td (7. Changeover procedure \(internal activities\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 585 Td (The changeover clock starts when the last good board of the previous job leaves the AOI. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 572 Td (line operator writes the start time on MFG-F-112. The target for a full changeover, from the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 559 Td (last good board of the previous job to QA release of the new job, is 25 minutes. Steps are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 546 Td (numbered continuously and must be performed in order unless a step explicitly allows parallel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 533 Td (work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 511 Td (1. Confirm on the Atlas shop-floor module that the previous job is complete and that the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 498 Td (   board count matches the job quantity. Record any shortfall on MFG-F-112.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 485 Td (2. Clear the line. Remove all boards of the previous job from the conveyors, the reflow oven) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 472 Td (   exit, the AOI buffer and the rework shelf. No board from the previous job may remain on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 459 Td (   the line when the first board of the new job is loaded.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 446 Td (3. Remove the stencil from the printer. Remove remaining paste from the stencil with the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 433 Td (   paste knife. Decide whether paste can be reused according to section 6.4; if not, scrap it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 420 Td (   and record the quantity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 407 Td (4. Send the used stencil to the stencil cleaner. The stencil is logged back into the stencil) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 394 Td (   store only after it has been cleaned and inspected.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 381 Td (5. Load the stencil for the new job. Scan the stencil ID barcode on the printer. The printer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 368 Td (   software rejects a stencil whose ID does not match the loaded print program.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 355 Td (6. Load the print program for the new board family. Confirm the under-stencil wipe frequency) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 342 Td (   in the program: every 5 prints for TS4E-EN, every 10 prints for HX-MB, TS4-GW and LF60-SB.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 329 Td (7. Apply fresh or reusable solder paste to the stencil. Confirm the open time written on the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 316 Td (   jar label is within 24 hours.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 303 Td (8. Remove the feeder carts of the previous job from both placement machines. At the same time) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 290 Td (   \(parallel work\), the material handler brings the pre-staged carts for the new job to the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 277 Td (   line.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 264 Td (9. Dock the pre-staged feeder carts to placement machine 1 and placement machine 2 according) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 251 Td (   to the cart labels.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 238 Td (10. Perform feeder verification. The line operator scans each feeder position against the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 225 Td (   setup sheet in the Atlas shop-floor module. Any mismatch between the scanned reel and the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 212 Td (   setup sheet locks the placement machine; the lock can only be released by correcting the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 199 Td (   feeder and rescanning, not by overriding on the machine.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 186 Td (11. Load the placement programs for both placement machines and the SPI and AOI programs for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 173 Td (   the new board family. Confirm the program names on the line PC match the traveller.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 160 Td (12. Load the reflow profile named on the traveller \(RP-HX-07, RP-GW-04, RP-TS4E-03 or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 147 Td (   RP-LF-02\). If the new profile is RP-TS4E-03, switch the oven to nitrogen and wait until) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 134 Td (   the oven O2 reading is below 1000 ppm. Wait for all 10 zones to reach their set points and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 121 Td (   for the oven to report stable. Record the oven stable time on MFG-F-112.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 108 Td (13. Adjust the conveyor width on printer, SPI, both placement machines, oven and AOI for the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 95 Td (   new board. Run one bare board through the whole line to confirm transfer without jamming.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 82 Td (14. Perform the First Article Inspection \(FAI\). Print, place and reflow the first board of the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 69 Td (   new job and hold it at the AOI output. The SPI result for the first board must show paste) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 56 Td (   volume within 75\226150% on every pad. The AOI false call rate for the new program is checked) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
