stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (   against the threshold of 500 ppm; if the false call rate is above 500 ppm, the AOI library) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (   must be re-tuned by the process engineer before release, and the FAI is repeated after) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (   re-tuning. The QA inspector performs the visual and dimensional checks listed in section) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 690 Td (   8. The FAI must be signed by QA on MFG-F-112 before the line is released. Without a QA) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 677 Td (   signature the line stays in FAI hold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 664 Td (15. If the SPI result is outside 75\226150% on any pad, stop. Check stencil seating, paste) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 651 Td (   condition and printer support pins, correct the cause, wash the board, and repeat step 14.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 638 Td (   Record each repeat on MFG-F-112.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 625 Td (16. If the AOI reports a real defect \(not a false call\) on the first article, the line lead) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 612 Td (   and QA inspector decide whether the cause is setup \(feeder, program, placement offset\) or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 599 Td (   material. Setup causes are corrected and step 14 is repeated. Material causes are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 586 Td (   escalated to the process engineer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 573 Td (17. The first article board is marked with the FAI label and retained at the line for the rest) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 560 Td (   of the shift. It is sent to the FAI retention shelf at the end of the shift.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 547 Td (18. Load a second board and confirm SPI and AOI results remain within the step 14 criteria.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 534 Td (   This confirms the setup is stable and not only correct for one board.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 521 Td (19. Before releasing the line to volume production, perform the two-person reflow profile) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 508 Td (   verification. The line lead and a second person \(the QA inspector or another qualified) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 495 Td (   setup technician\) independently read the profile name loaded on the oven controller and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 482 Td (   compare it with the profile named on the job traveller. Both people initial MFG-F-112. If) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 469 Td (   the names differ, the line must not be released; all boards processed since step 12 are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 456 Td (   quarantined and the line lead contacts the process engineer. This step was added as an) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 443 Td (   action item of postmortem INC-2025-014, when SMT-2 ran TS4E-EN boards on the HX-MB profile) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 430 Td (   \(RP-HX-07 instead of RP-TS4E-03\) in March 2025.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 417 Td (20. Release the line in the Atlas shop-floor module. The release transaction records the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 404 Td (   operator, line lead and QA inspector IDs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 391 Td (21. Record the changeover end time on MFG-F-112. The changeover time is the elapsed time from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 378 Td (   the start time recorded before step 1 to the release in step 20.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 365 Td (22. If the changeover time exceeded 25 minutes, record the main cause of delay on MFG-F-112) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 352 Td (   using the delay codes in section 10. If it exceeded 40 minutes, confirm the shift lead was) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 339 Td (   contacted \(see section 9\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 326 Td (23. Return unused reels from the previous job to stores. Each reel is scanned back into Atlas.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 313 Td (   MSL reels are returned with an updated floor life label or placed into dry storage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 300 Td (   according to mfg-msl-handling-procedure.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 287 Td (24. Return the feeder carts from the previous job to the pre-staging bench. Unload the feeders) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 274 Td (   and clean them before they are reused.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 261 Td (25. Confirm that the paste jar in use is labelled with the line number and open time, and that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 248 Td (   the next paste required for the shift has been removed from the refrigerator in time to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 235 Td (   complete its 4-hour thaw.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 222 Td (26. Clean the work area around the printer and placement machines. Remove any dropped) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 209 Td (   components; dropped components are scrapped, never reloaded.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 196 Td (27. Check the SPI trend for the first 20 boards. If paste volume is trending towards the 75%) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 183 Td (   or 150% limits, notify the line lead before the limit is reached.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 170 Td (28. Check the AOI false call trend for the first 50 boards. If the false call rate trends) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 157 Td (   above 500 ppm, notify the process engineer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 144 Td (29. The line lead reviews MFG-F-112 for completeness: start time, stencil ID and tension) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 131 Td (   reading, feeder verification result, profile and oven stable time, FAI signature, step 19) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 118 Td (   initials, release time and delay codes.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 105 Td (30. The line lead submits MFG-F-112. Completed forms are scanned and attached to the job in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 92 Td (   the Atlas shop-floor module at the end of the shift.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 76 Td (8. First article inspection acceptance criteria) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 54 Td (The QA inspector uses the following criteria for the FAI in step 14. All criteria must be met) Tj ET
endstream
